  "summary": "New portals, databases and workflows harmonize spatial and single-cell data at scale, shifting emphasis from individual datasets to reusable, traceable…",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is infrastructure that consolidates heterogeneous spatial and single-cell data and standardizes access. The HuBMAP Data Portal hosts 9,316 public datasets from healthy human tissues, and STRAND harmonizes 35 subcellular-resolution spatial transcriptomics datasets (~4.9 billion transcript coordinates). SpaceBlocks provides a Snakemake workflow for reproducible, expert-supervised cohort-level analysis. TRACE emphasizes traceable curation, demonstrated on a harmonised single-cell glaucoma resource, and NLM-CKN links data-driven cell phenotypes across 88 datasets to Cell Ontology, genes, diseases and drugs. PathoEvo, SENgEAR and CircaVal apply interactive database approaches to disease progression, senescence and circadian regulation, and are less specifically spatial. Gene Embedding Hub, PhenoMe and QUEST extend the theme to embeddings and virtual staining. The contribution is integration, provenance and access rather than new inference methods.",
